================================================================================
Educational Use & Authorization Notice
================================================================================

This lab (bufoverflow) is **buffer-overflow teaching material** that reproduces
the publicly documented Aleph One paper *Smashing The Stack For Fun And Profit*
(Phrack 49-14, 1996), ported to modern x86_64 Linux. Its sole purpose is
**education and defensive research**.

Scope of authorized use
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Use only on systems and processes you **own or are explicitly authorized**
  (in writing) to test.
- All targets here run **locally, unprivileged, attacking your own process**.
- The attack vector is a local `argv[1]`; there is **no network service**. The
  resulting shell inherits the current user's identity and provides **no
  privilege escalation, persistence, lateral movement, or remote capability**.
- The exploitable target **does not occur naturally**: it must be deliberately
  compiled with `-O0 -fno-stack-protector -no-pie -z execstack`. Any normally
  built binary is stopped by any one of those mitigations — which is exactly
  what this lab teaches.

Prohibited use
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Do **not** use any code, payload, or technique from this lab against systems you
are not authorized to test, against production environments, against other
people's equipment, or in any way that violates applicable law. Responsibility
for misuse rests entirely with the user.

